From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000017 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: cubie-a7s: look for U-Boot where binman puts it

On the A733, binman places the FIT 0x4a000 bytes after the start of the
SPL: that is the min-size of the SPL entry in sunxi-u-boot.dtsi
(cc66811f4f). The SPL looks for the FIT max(SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR,
eGON length / 512) sectors after its own start
(board_spl_mmc_get_uboot_raw_sector()), the eGON length being the SPL
rounded up to 8 KiB. With the default 0x40 both meet only while the SPL
is larger than 0x48000 bytes, and dropping the SPL's UFS and SPI-NOR
loaders makes it smaller. 0x250 is 0x4a000 / 512, the value the comment
in sunxi-u-boot.dtsi asks for, so the SPL finds the FIT whatever its own
size.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
index ee7cab41282..c145d3381c2 100644
--- a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
+++ b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
@@ -64,6 +64,7 @@ CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET=y
 CONFIG_USB_ETH_CDC=y
 CONFIG_SPL_STACK_R_MALLOC_SIMPLE_LEN=0x140000
+CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR=0x250
 CONFIG_PCI=y
 CONFIG_NVME_PCI=y
 CONFIG_PCIE_SUNXI=y
